cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "linkoutage: outage and availability statistics for an optical link"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Fade statistics of an optical link computed from a supplied or generated
  amplitude series, with every definitional choice explicit and reported
  alongside the numbers: down-crossing count, level-crossing rate, fade
  durations with left and right censoring, outage fraction and availability
  under seven stated conventions whose spread on a two-million-sample record is
  measured rather than assumed. Fade-duration distribution fitting with a
  goodness-of-fit verdict on the memoryless hypothesis, tested by a Pearson
  chi-square on the discrete sample-count histogram rather than by a
  Kolmogorov-Smirnov test against a continuous law, with a positive control on
  truly geometric data. Two-state and N-state Markov and semi-Markov
  channel-state fitting with a dwell-time chi-square, a conditional-independence
  test of the Markov property and its effect size. A short-horizon outage
  classifier benchmarked against three baselines, including the constant
  base-rate forecaster, with calibration reported as a Brier decomposition,
  expected calibration error and reliability curves rather than as accuracy.
  Exact discrete-time analytic level-crossing rate and mean fade duration for
  the correlated lognormal channel, computed two independent ways. Validation
  level 2, research grade. Not flight-qualified, not certified, not approved
  for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - free-space-optical
  - fade-statistics
  - level-crossing-rate
  - mean-fade-duration
  - outage-probability
  - availability
  - lognormal-fading
  - scintillation
  - markov-channel
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Rice
        given-names: "S. O."
    title: "Mathematical analysis of random noise"
    journal: "Bell System Technical Journal"
    year: 1945
    notes: >-
      The level-crossing problem and the relation between the crossing rate of
      a level, the fraction of time spent below it and the mean duration of an
      excursion. Published in two parts, 1944 and 1945. This repository uses
      the discrete-record form of that relation as an internal consistency
      check and does not quote any equation number or page from the original.
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Andrews
        given-names: "L. C."
      - family-names: Phillips
        given-names: "R. L."
    title: "Laser Beam Propagation through Random Media"
    edition: "2nd"
    publisher:
      name: "SPIE Press"
    year: 2005
    notes: >-
      The lognormal irradiance model for weak-to-moderate scintillation used in
      linkoutage.channel, and the scintillation index as the parameter of that
      model. This repository implements the lognormal distribution and an AR(1)
      temporal correlation; it does not implement the propagation theory that
      produces the scintillation index from turbulence strength and path
      geometry.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Gilbert
        given-names: "E. N."
    title: "Capacity of a burst-noise channel"
    journal: "Bell System Technical Journal"
    year: 1960
    notes: >-
      The two-state burst channel named in linkoutage.markov. Gilbert's channel
      attaches an error process to the states; this repository fits only the
      state process.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Al-Habash
        given-names: "M. A."
      - family-names: Andrews
        given-names: "L. C."
      - family-names: Phillips
        given-names: "R. L."
    title: >-
      Mathematical model for the irradiance probability density function of a
      laser beam propagating through turbulent media
    journal: "Optical Engineering"
    volume: 40
    issue: 8
    start: 1554
    end: 1562
    year: 2001
    notes: >-
      The gamma-gamma irradiance distribution, named in this repository's
      limitations as the standard replacement for the lognormal model in strong
      turbulence. It is NOT implemented here.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Murphy
        given-names: "A. H."
    title: "A new vector partition of the probability score"
    journal: "Journal of Applied Meteorology"
    volume: 12
    issue: 4
    start: 595
    end: 600
    year: 1973
    notes: >-
      The reliability-resolution-uncertainty decomposition of the Brier score
      implemented in linkoutage.calibration.brier_decomposition.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Kaplan
        given-names: "E. L."
      - family-names: Meier
        given-names: "P."
    title: "Nonparametric estimation from incomplete observations"
    journal: "Journal of the American Statistical Association"
    volume: 53
    issue: 282
    start: 457
    end: 481
    year: 1958
    notes: >-
      The product-limit survival estimator implemented in
      linkoutage.distributions.kaplan_meier_survival.
